# Keep the deploy payload small. Without this the CLI uploads data/ (~19 MB of
# source CSVs) on every deploy, which is slow enough to time out.
# Only what the running service needs should ship: api/, src/, static/, and the
# ONE script the runtime imports.
#
# ⚠️ The daily-intelligence cron does `from scripts import isd_intel` at request
# time (src/api.py). Excluding all of scripts/ makes that ImportError in
# production and the feed can never refresh past its committed snapshot. So ship
# the package marker + that one module, and nothing else from scripts/.
# data/* not data/ — gitignore semantics (which .vercelignore follows) cannot
# re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, so `data/` plus
# `!data/district_crosswalk.csv` would silently keep excluding it. Same shape
# as the scripts/* rule below, for the same reason.
data/*
docs/
#
# ⚠️ src/sources.py reads scripts/freshness_vintages.json at request time, to
# answer "is this source still current?" on the lineage panel. Without it the
# answer degrades to "we do not know" — which is the honest fallback, and is
# also indistinguishable from a working deploy unless you click a number. That
# is exactly this project's recurring failure: a check pointed slightly to the
# left of the thing it describes. tests/test_lineage.py fails the build if this
# re-include disappears.
scripts/*
!scripts/__init__.py
!scripts/isd_intel.py
!scripts/freshness_vintages.json
tests/
sql/
.github/
.claude/
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
*.png
# …except the one image the API serves: the TAG graphic the outreach emails
# hot-link at /static/tag-pipeline.png. A blanket *.png silently 404s it.
!static/tag_pipeline.png
# Per-district social cards (built by scripts/build_share_cards.py).
!static/share/*.png
#
# ⚠️ src/outreach_map.py reads data/district_crosswalk.csv at request time, to
# name each district on the private outreach map. Without it /ops/outreach-data
# raised FileNotFoundError and answered 500 — in production only, from the day
# it shipped, while every test stayed green because the repo checkout HAS the
# file. This is the third time this exact shape has bitten (scripts/isd_intel,
# scripts/freshness_vintages.json, now this): anything under src/ that opens a
# file outside src//static//api/ needs a re-include AND a test.
# It must come after BOTH `data/*` and `*.csv`, or those re-exclude it.
!data/district_crosswalk.csv
#
# src/outreach_runner.py reads these two committed files at request time:
# the watermark is the re-send floor, the suppression list the dead-address
# block. Both are hashes/counts, never contact data. Same rule as the
# crosswalk re-include above: anything src/ opens outside src//static//api/
# needs a re-include AND tests/test_vercelignore.py enforces it.
!data/outreach_watermark.json
!data/outreach_suppression.json
*.ipynb
Dockerfile
render.yaml
scratchpad/
